# Landsat-5 TM Input Data

The study used Landsat-5 Thematic Mapper (TM) Collection 2 Level 2 Surface Reflectance data obtained from the U.S. Geological Survey (USGS) EarthExplorer.

## Scene used

Scene ID:

LT05_L2SP_140045_19910320_20200915_02_T1_SR

Acquisition date:

20 March 1991

Spatial resolution:

30 m

## Bands used

The following six reflective bands were used in the classification:

- B1 – Blue
- B2 – Green
- B3 – Red
- B4 – Near Infrared (NIR)
- B5 – Shortwave Infrared 1 (SWIR 1)
- B7 – Shortwave Infrared 2 (SWIR 2)

The study-area raster filenames were:

- L5TM_19910320_AOI_SR_B1.tif
- L5TM_19910320_AOI_SR_B2.tif
- L5TM_19910320_AOI_SR_B3.tif
- L5TM_19910320_AOI_SR_B4.tif
- L5TM_19910320_AOI_SR_B5.tif
- L5TM_19910320_AOI_SR_B7.tif

## Data availability

The original Landsat-5 TM scene is publicly available from USGS EarthExplorer using the scene ID given above.

The full study-area GeoTIFF rasters are not stored directly in this GitHub repository because of repository/browser file-size limitations.

These six bands were the input raster datasets used for the ArcMap and QGIS/SCP classifications reported in the manuscript.
